---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
import { hooksDiagram } from '../data/diagrams';
---

<DocsLayout title="Hooks" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="hooks">

  <div class="panel-intro">
    <h2>Hooks</h2>
    <p>Hooks are <strong>automatic safety checks</strong> that run behind the scenes at zero token cost. When an agent tries to write a file or run a command, hooks intercept the action and validate it before it executes. Think of them as security guards at every door &mdash; they check permissions instantly using small bash scripts, not AI processing.</p>
    <div class="key-points">
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What they are</strong>
          <p>Bash scripts triggered by Claude Code lifecycle events (session start, before/after tool use, session end). They read a JSON payload from stdin and return exit code 0 (allow) or 2 (block).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
          <p>AI models can forget rules mid-session. Hooks enforce constraints deterministically &mdash; the phase gate blocks source code writes before the foundation is complete, the quality gate catches build errors, and the data protector blocks destructive commands. No token cost, no forgetting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Session Init Hooks</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">Run automatically when a new Claude Code session starts.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Script</th><th>Event</th><th>What It Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>session-startup.sh</code></td>
          <td>SessionStart</td>
          <td>Checks environment (Git, Node, jq), detects terminal type, loads state, and routes to the right workflow.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>sync-state.sh</code></td>
          <td>SessionStart</td>
          <td>Reconciles state files on startup &mdash; ensures <code>.vibecrew/</code> JSON is consistent after crashes or manual edits.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>error-recovery.sh</code></td>
          <td>SessionStart</td>
          <td>Clears stale lock files and repairs corrupted state from previous interrupted sessions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>compact-reinject.sh</code></td>
          <td>SessionStart (compact)</td>
          <td>Re-injects essential context (active feature, phase, conventions) after Claude Code's <code>/compact</code> clears the context window.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Pre-Action Guards</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">Intercept actions before they execute. Return exit code 2 to block.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Script</th><th>Event</th><th>What It Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>phase-gate.sh</code></td>
          <td>PreToolUse (Write/Edit)</td>
          <td>Blocks source code writes until the Tier 1 foundation (VISION, TDR, architecture, CLAUDE.md) is complete. Prevents coding before decisions are made.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>restrict-paths.sh</code></td>
          <td>PreToolUse (Write/Edit)</td>
          <td>Blocks file writes outside the project root directory. Prevents agents from modifying system files or other projects.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>protect-data.sh</code></td>
          <td>PreToolUse (Bash)</td>
          <td>Blocks destructive shell commands: <code>rm -rf</code>, <code>DROP TABLE</code>, <code>DELETE FROM</code> without WHERE, force push, and privilege escalation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>validate-phase-transition.sh</code></td>
          <td>PreToolUse (Bash)</td>
          <td>Enforces phase ordering &mdash; ensures foundation steps run in sequence and artifacts are complete before advancing.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>validate-signal.sh</code></td>
          <td>PreToolUse (Write/Edit)</td>
          <td>Validates inter-agent signal file schemas, enum values, and feature ID cross-references before they're written.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Post-Action Processors</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">Run after an action completes successfully.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Script</th><th>Event</th><th>What It Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>format-code.sh</code></td>
          <td>PostToolUse (Write/Edit)</td>
          <td>Auto-formats files after every write using the project's configured formatter (Prettier, ESLint, etc.).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>notify.sh</code></td>
          <td>Notification / PostToolUseFailure</td>
          <td>Sends native OS notifications for permission stalls, task completions, and errors. Includes Warp Terminal deep-links when available.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Session End Checks</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">Run when a session stops to catch issues before they persist.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Script</th><th>Event</th><th>What It Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>quality-gate.sh</code></td>
          <td>Stop</td>
          <td>Runs typecheck, lint, and build on modified source files. Blocks task completion if any check fails &mdash; the agent must fix errors before finishing.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>claude-md-lint.sh</code></td>
          <td>Stop</td>
          <td>Validates CLAUDE.md file size and structure. Keeps it under the recommended line limit to avoid context bloat.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>cost-guardrails.sh</code></td>
          <td>Stop</td>
          <td>Tracks session and daily API costs against configured thresholds. Warns or blocks when spending exceeds limits.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>check-context.sh</code></td>
          <td>Stop</td>
          <td>Monitors context window usage and warns at 45% and 60%. Helps prevent sessions from running out of context mid-task.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <MermaidDiagram chart={hooksDiagram} caption="Hook events mapped to their enforcement scripts" />

</DocsLayout>
